@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

#
# prima-materia — chaos magic: Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:ChaosMagic, kept apart from
# traditions/chaos-magic.ttl, which declares the tradition and the work
# (pmw:OvenReadyChaos). Edition: Phil Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4,
# the on-line edition typeset by the author and converted to TealDOC by
# Yiri T. Kohl (readme dated 14 June 2000), read from the archive.org item
# tucows_72598_oven_ready_chaos with the PalmDOC files decoded. The text
# says it was first published by Chaos International Publications in 1992,
# in an edition of 300, under the title Condensed Chaos, and renamed on-line
# to avoid confusion with the New Falcon book of 1995; the main text is
# signed March 1992, and version 1.4 adds two appendices. Cited by section
# heading and item number; the text has no pages.
#
# The New Falcon book Condensed Chaos (1995, pmw:CondensedChaos, harvested in
# traditions/chaos-magic-condensed-chaos.ttl) grew out of this text. The same
# assertion by the same author is not entered twice: every item of the
# harvest was compared with the nodes of that file, and where the 1995 node
# carries the claim, no node is written here (the mapping is kept with the
# harvest note). A node stands here when the 1992 text carries a claim no
# node of the 1995 harvest carries (the Discordian material, the Discordian
# Opening Ritual, the spiral pentagrams, most of the appendix essays), or
# when it states a claim in a different form; such a node carries a note
# beginning "Differs from" that names the 1995 node and the difference.
# Links into claims already carried point at the 1995 nodes.
#
# Harvested under prima-materia#893 with two independent extraction passes,
# reconciled by offset and word overlap. Signs of success and conditions of
# failure carry a note beginning "Counted as a sign of success:" or
# "Counted as a condition of failure:".
#


#
# What is Magick?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAgainstObscurantistOccultism a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against obscurantist occultism of inner planes and hierarchies"@en, "Gegen obskurantistischen Okkultismus von inneren Ebenen und Hierarchien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine objects that magick has been smothered in technical vocabulary that shuts out outsiders and props up pomposity, and that towering schemes of inner worlds, ranked spiritual beings and secret doctrines have made people forget that the surrounding world is magical."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the occultism he opposes is described, not quoted from any named work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), What is Magick?; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMagickSimpleWorldMagical a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magick is simple; the world is magical"@en, "Magie ist einfach; die Welt ist magisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine holds that magick is at bottom simple and that the mystery lies in the living world about us, a world he calls magical, rather than in lost tongues, graves or hidden lore; magick is a door into mystery, wildness and immanence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), What is Magick?; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# What is Chaos Magick?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAgainstSystemsApproach a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the Systems approach"@en, "Gegen den System-Ansatz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine criticises the dominant Systems approach for making the student absorb beliefs, rules, correspondences and even dress codes before doing any magic, and argues that simple ideas there harden into complicated beliefs that lead away from practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: no exponent of the Systems approach is named or quoted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), What is Chaos Magick?; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMagicalSystem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical system"@en, "Magisches System"@de ;
    skos:definition "A magical system is described as combining practical change techniques with beliefs, attitudes, one or more models of the universe, a moral ethic and more; examples given are Qabalah, Wiccan traditions, the Golden Dawn and westernised shamanic paths."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), What is Chaos Magick?; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHumourMissingFromMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Humour missing from magic (Discordian point)"@en, "Fehlender Humor in der Magie (diskordischer Punkt)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Discordians are reported as pointing out that humour and light-heartedness were missing from magic, which tended toward seriousness, self-importance and an initiated-elite self-image."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported from Robert Anton Wilson and the Discordian Society; Hine adds that occultists tended to see themselves as an initiated elite."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), What is Chaos Magick?; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations
#

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcOwnMagicalSystem a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating one's own magical system (D.I.Y.)"@en, "Eigenes magisches System erschaffen (D.I.Y.)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine recommends building one's own operationally valid magical system, as Austin Osman Spare did, rather than repeating others' rituals and ideas; whether others can work it is secondary."@en ;
    skos:note "Spare cited as model."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, D.I.Y; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcOwnSystemYieldsConfidence a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own-system work yields confidence"@en, "Arbeit am eigenen System erzeugt Selbstvertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Original, self-devised magical work is said to build the practitioner's confidence."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcOwnMagicalSystem ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcConfidenceFromInnovation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, D.I.Y; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcConfidenceFromInnovation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence from innovation"@en, "Selbstvertrauen durch Innovation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doing something innovative, especially if no one one knows has tried it, is said to be very good for building confidence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, D.I.Y; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcWrongPentagramsNothingNoticed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual error without consequence (anecdote)"@en, "Ritualfehler ohne Folgen (Anekdote)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine recalls realising he had drawn all the pentagrams wrongly in a ritual and that nothing noticed or turned up, offered as an indication that formal correctness matters less than assumed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, D.I.Y; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMetasystems a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Metasystems"@en, "Metasysteme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Metasystems are attempts to build a frame into which everything can be slotted, such as merging runes with tarot or mapping all onto the Tree of Life; Hine calls this a often useful and fun exercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, Metasystems; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSpuriousNecronomiconResults a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spurious Necronomicon still yielded reported results"@en, "Gefälschtes Necronomicon brachte dennoch berichtete Ergebnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine relates that an occult author published a spurious version of the Necronomicon and was sent many letters by people who had performed its rituals and wished to discuss their results; he ties this to belief as a magical tool."@en ;
    skos:note "Author unnamed in the text."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, Metasystems; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHineSystemHopping a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hine's own system-hopping"@en, "Hines eigener Systemwechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine says he switches among his own D.I.Y. work, Qabalah, Tantra, the Cthulhu Mythos, Shamanism and other systems as seems fitting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, Metasystems; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCompetenceInOneSystem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Competence and confidence in one system"@en, "Kompetenz und Sicherheit in einem System"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working a system in some depth is said to make one more or less competent and confident in it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, Metasystems; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDepthInOneSystemFirst a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Depth in one system before others"@en, "Tiefe in einem System vor weiteren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Competence in a first system is presented as easing the acquisition of further ones."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCompetenceInOneSystem ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicOrcEaseWithFurtherSystems ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, Metasystems; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcEaseWithFurtherSystems a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ease in learning further systems"@en, "Leichtigkeit beim Erlernen weiterer Systeme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once competent in one system, magicians are said to find it easier to master another; experience with Enochian, for example, should ease work with the Runes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, Metasystems; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcInformationFieldsBecomeEntities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Information fields becoming autonomous entities"@en, "Informationsfelder, die zu autonomen Wesenheiten werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing Chaos Servitors: A User Guide, Hine says localised information fields may in time self-organise until they are experienced as autonomous entities, i.e. spirits, so that the Cybernetic model loops back to the Spirit model."@en ;
    skos:note "Refers to a separate work (Hine's own Chaos Servitors booklet, author not named here)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Infinite Diversity / Infinite Combinations, Magical Models; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# All Hail Discordia!
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcEvenFalseThingsTrue a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everything is true, even false things"@en, "Alles ist wahr, auch Falsches"@de ;
    skos:definition "A quoted Discordian dialogue has Malaclypse affirm that everything, including false things, is true, and disclaim responsibility for it."@en ;
    skos:note "A dialogue between Malaclypse and a 'Greater Poop', quoted without source in the text; the Principia Discordia is named just before it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), All Hail Discordia!; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcEveryoneAGenuinePope a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyone a genuine Pope"@en, "Jeder ein echter Papst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Discordian movement is said to spread partly through its tactic of declaring every person a genuine Pope, as a religion celebrating confusion and madness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), All Hail Discordia!; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Discordian Opening Ritual
#

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcDiscordianOpeningRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Discordian Opening Ritual"@en, "Diskordisches Eröffnungsritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: clap five times; perform the Erisian Cross, placing light in the head, fire in the genitals, strength at the right, laughter at the left and love in the heart; trace spiral pentagrams at the four quarters and zenith; facing east, south, west, north, then up or down, call in turn on the Apostles Hung Mung, Van Van Mojo, Sri Syadasti, Zarathud and Malaclypse for their gifts; looking all around, invoke Eris for liberty, love, light and life and for the magick to work; close with a hail to Eris and Discordia."@en ;
    skos:note "The rite is headed 'by Prince Prance'; Hine afterwards calls it a variant of the centering (banishing) rite, pmp:ChaosMagicOrcCenteringRite. Condensed Chaos (1995) does not carry this rite."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, items 1-10; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcGiftsOfTheApostles a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gifts asked of the Discordian Apostles"@en, "Von den diskordischen Aposteln erbetene Gaben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The calls ask for balance and equilibrium, voodoo power and confusion of enemies, relative truth and mind-expansion, Erisian doubt and Chaos's constancy, illumination and protection from stupidity, and from Eris liberty, love, light and life and that the magick work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, items 4-9; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcOpeningRitualYieldsGifts a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Opening Ritual petitions its gifts"@en, "Eröffnungsritual erbittet seine Gaben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Discordian Opening Ritual is framed as obtaining the gifts named in its invocations."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcDiscordianOpeningRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcGiftsOfTheApostles ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHungMungNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Hung Mung"@en, "Hung Mung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blessed Apostle and great Sage of Cathay, Discordianism's connection with the Chinese Mysteries and deviser of the Sacred Chao; patron of Chaos, the first season; invoked in the east for balance."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Hung Mung" ;
    pm:nameRole "Discordian Apostle of the East; patron of the Season of Chaos" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, item 4 and note 1; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDiscordianSeasonPatrons a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five Discordian seasons and their patrons"@en, "Fünf diskordische Jahreszeiten und ihre Patrone"@de ;
    skos:definition "The notes to the Opening Ritual give each of the five Apostles invoked a Discordian season as patron: Hung Mung of Chaos, Van Van Mojo of Discord, Sri Syadasti of Confusion, Zarathud of Bureaucracy, Malaclypse the Elder of Aftermath."@en ;
    skos:note "The seasons are those of the Discordian calendar; the order of the patrons follows the order of the calls (east, south, west, north, above or below). Kept as an ordering of the notes, not as a series, because no patron has its sense from its place."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Prince Prance, in the notes to the Discordian Opening Ritual printed by Hine" ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, notes 1-5; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcVanVanMojoNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Dr. Van Van Mojo"@en, "Dr. Van Van Mojo"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blessed Apostle and Doctor of Hoodoo and Vexes, member of an intergalactic Haitian guerilla fellowship for world peace; patron of Discord, the second season; invoked in the south for voodoo power."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Van Van Mojo" ;
    pm:nameRole "Discordian Apostle of the South; patron of the Season of Discord" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, item 5 and note 2; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSriSyadastiNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Sri Syadasti"@en, "Sri Syadasti"@de ;
    skos:definition "Apostle and patron of psychedelia and of Confusion, the third season; invoked in the west to teach relative truth."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Sri Syadasti" ;
    pm:nameRole "Discordian Apostle of the West; patron of the Season of Confusion" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, item 6 and note 3; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcZarathudNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Zarathud"@en, "Zarathud"@de ;
    skos:definition "A hard-nosed medieval European hermit called \"Offender of the Faith\"; patron of Bureaucracy, the fourth season; invoked in the north for Erisian doubt."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Zarathud" ;
    pm:nameRole "Discordian Apostle of the North; patron of Bureaucracy, the fourth season" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, item 7 and note 4; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMalaclypseTheElderNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Malaclypse the Elder"@en, "Malaclypse der Ältere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elder Saint of Discordia, alleged ancient wise man who bore a placard reading DUMB through the back streets of Rome, Mecca, Baghdad and Jerusalem; patron of Aftermath, the fifth season; invoked above or below for illumination."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Malaclypse the Elder" ;
    pm:nameRole "Discordian Elder Saint, zenith/nadir; patron of the Season of Aftermath" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Discordian Opening Ritual, item 8 and note 5; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Spiral Pentagrams
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcTraditionalPentagramBanishing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Traditional pentagram suits banishing"@en, "Das traditionelle Pentagramm eignet sich zum Bannen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine finds the traditional pentagram a very solid geometric figure and its link to banishing apt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagram a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing the Spiral Pentagram"@en, "Zeichnen des Spiralpentagramms"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trace in the air a five-pointed star formed of curves whose centre repeats the petal shape; while drawing, visualise the outer petals turning clockwise and the inner ones anticlockwise, the whole becoming a three-dimensional tunnel twisting off into infinite space."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's own figure; he says it is hard to trace in the air at first and asks readers for reports of their use of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagramYieldsDrawingIn a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spiral Pentagrams draw energies in; first trial worked"@en, "Spiralpentagramme ziehen Energien herein; erster Versuch gelang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Their first use, in a working invoking Eris, is reported to have worked very well, drawing energies in."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagram ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDrawingEnergiesIn ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDrawingEnergiesIn a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing energies in"@en, "Hereinziehen von Energien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike banishing pentagrams, spiral pentagrams are said not to keep things out but to draw energies in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagramGating a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gating through Spiral Pentagrams in astral work"@en, "Durchschreiten von Spiralpentagrammen in Astralarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In astral projection (\"Virtual Magick\") the spiral pentagram can serve as a gate to pass through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralGatingYieldsDoorway a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spiral gating yields astral doorway"@en, "Spiraltor ergibt astrales Tor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Used in astral projection the figure serves as a doorway."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagramGating ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAstralDoorway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAstralDoorway a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astral doorway"@en, "Astrales Tor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spiral pentagrams act as gateways in astral work; Hine reports them appearing unbidden in his dreams as astral doorways."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSealingSpiralPentagram a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sealing a Spiral Pentagram"@en, "Versiegeln eines Spiralpentagramms"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reverse the spin of the petals and let the figure flatten again; Hine sometimes traces an ordinary pentagram over it as well."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagramTradSystemsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spiral Pentagrams fail with traditional systems"@en, "Spiralpentagramme versagen in traditionellen Systemen"@de ;
    skos:definition "They are said to work in free-form workings but not with traditional systems like the Solomonic Lesser Key, whose entities Hine finds conservative about how they are evoked."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the spiral pentagrams are said to work in free-form workings and not with traditional systems, Hine's instance being the Lesser Key of Solomon. Cause: the entities of the traditional system, which Hine finds strictly conservative about how they are evoked, not the operator. No deadline and no rate; hedged with 'seem'. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSpiralPentagram."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcProcessVersusContent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Process versus content"@en, "Prozess versus Inhalt"@de ;
    skos:definition "An early tenet of the Chaos current holds that ritual content is somewhat arbitrary while the underlying process is what matters; different rites with different content follow the same process."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on what in the method is fixed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCenteringRitesNullPoint a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering (banishing) rituals"@en, "Zentrierungs-(Bannungs-)Rituale"@de ;
    skos:definition "Centering rites aim to set the magician at the centre of his psychocosm, the world-axis or zero point that all magic starts from; they warm one up for entering a space where nothing is true and everything permitted."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering (Condensed Chaos, 1995): Condensed Chaos (ch. 4, p. 77) gives centering as a practice with three core steps and a range from full banishing to a moment of no-mind; the 1992 text instead states the purpose of the centering rite (the centre of one's psychocosm, the axis mundi or null-point) and its function as a warm-up for the main working, with the Discordian Opening Ritual as its example."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCentredAndReturning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being centred and returning to consensus reality"@en, "Zentriertsein und Rückkehr in die Konsensrealität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Centering places one at the null-point for magical work and, repeated afterwards, readies one to return to everyday consensus reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBeingCentredPoised (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 node is being relaxed and poised at the centre of one's magical reality; the 1992 text adds the second performance after the working, which readies one to go back into consensus reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcCenteringRite a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering/banishing rite (common process)"@en, "Zentrierungs-/Bannungsritus (gemeinsamer Ablauf)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Combine gesture, voice, breath and visualisation to mark the four cardinal quarters and a fifth point standing for union with Kia, chaos or spirit; do it before the main working and once more afterwards, the second time to prepare the return to consensus reality. The standard Lesser Banishing Ritual of the Pentagram and the IOT's Gnostic Banishing are named as instances."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 practice has three steps (bodily presence, gates or quarters, identification with a source of inspiration); the 1992 rite names gesture, voice, breath and visualisation, the four quarters with a fifth point for Kia, chaos or spirit, performance before and again after the main working, and the Lesser Banishing Ritual of the Pentagram and the IOT Gnostic Banishing as instances."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCenteringRiteYieldsCentring a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Centering rite yields centring and shift"@en, "Zentrierungsritus ergibt Zentrierung und Übergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Centering rites produce centring, an atmospheric change and, with practice, an automatic felt shift into magical reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCenteringYieldsPoiseYield (Condensed Chaos, 1995): In 1995 centering yields relaxation and readiness for action; in 1992 the rite yields being centred, a change of atmosphere in the place, and with practice a felt shift into magical reality that sets in by itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcCenteringRite, pmp:ChaosMagicOrcDiscordianOpeningRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCentredAndReturning, pmc:ChaosMagicOrcConditionedShiftIntoMagicalReality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAtmosphereChangeSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Atmospheric change and automatic onset of feelings"@en, "Atmosphärische Veränderung und automatisches Einsetzen der Gefühle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Signs that the rite works: a change in the felt atmosphere of the space and, after practice, the feelings coming on of themselves whenever the rite begins."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the atmosphere of the place changes, and after practice the accompanying feelings set in automatically each time the rite is performed. Judged by the operator alone; no deadline, the second sign comes only 'with practice'. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicOrcCenteringRite."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBRelaxedPreparedPoisedSign (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 sign is feeling relaxed, ready and poised; the 1992 signs are a change in the felt atmosphere of the place and, after practice, the feelings arising of themselves whenever the rite is begun."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcConditionedShiftIntoMagicalReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conditioned shift into magical reality"@en, "Konditionierter Übergang in die magische Realität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Such rites change the atmosphere of the place, and with practice the accompanying feelings arise automatically each time the rite is performed, so the shift between everyday and magical reality is clearly felt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Spiral Pentagrams; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


