#
# Basic Exercises
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcBasicExercisesStatus a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Status of the basic exercises"@en, "Status der Grundübungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercises are said to be compiled from various sources and to have perhaps little value in themselves, though they may be fun and have far-reaching consequences."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed or tested the methods are."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcBornAgainAdoptedBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Adopted belief that stayed (Born-Again anecdote)"@en, "Übernommener Glaube, der blieb (Wiedergeborenen-Anekdote)"@de ;
    skos:definition "An acquaintance began Chaos magick by adopting the belief system of a Born-Again Christian; he has remained one, but seems happier."@en ;
    skos:note "Told as a joke: the belief adopted as an experiment was never dropped."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcSeveralExplanations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Multiple explanations for every result"@en, "Mehrere Erklärungen für jedes Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "For any magical result, failures included, think up several explanations, at least one in terms of the magical system used, one strictly materialist, and one exceedingly silly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 1; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcBeliefShiftingBeforeExclusivePairs a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief-shifting experience before contradictory pairs"@en, "Erfahrung im Glaubenswechsel vor widersprüchlichen Paaren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The contradictory-belief contemplation is to follow a period of experiment with belief-shifting."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondCChakraBeliefShift ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicOrcContemplatingExclusiveBeliefs ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 2; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcContemplatingExclusiveBeliefs a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Contemplating mutually exclusive beliefs"@en, "Betrachtung einander ausschließender Glaubenssysteme"@de ;
    skos:definition "After some time belief-shifting, contemplate two systems that seem mutually exclusive, e.g. Christianity with Tantra, Islam with radical feminism, Celtic revivalism with Marxism."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 2; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMeditationsInMenzies a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditations in Menzies"@en, "Meditationen bei Menzies"@de ;
    skos:definition "Read specialist magazines on subjects of no interest to you, especially amateur enthusiasts' ones, and read publications of opposed views one after another (e.g. a men's magazine and a feminist one, Dworkin and de Sade)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 3; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcNoLiveToadsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No live toads in the mouth"@en, "Keine lebenden Kröten in den Mund"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reader is told not to put live toads in the mouth."@en ;
    skos:note "Item 4 of the basic exercises, given without explanation; it is a joke, and what it alludes to is not stated."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicOrcBasicExercisesStatus ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 4; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcEveryoneElseABuddha a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyone is a buddha but you"@en, "Alle sind Buddhas außer dir"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hold the attitude that everyone else is a buddha waiting for you to sort yourself out, buddhahood showing most in those you avoid in the street, and act accordingly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 5; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcBeingConsistentlyWrong a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Being consistently wrong"@en, "Konsequent falsch liegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make wild statements and, when someone refutes them, admit the mistake, profusely if need be; one may err about the hour, the weekday, political claims and so on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 6; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcPossessionAndGurusConfidence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession and gurus grant confidence"@en, "Besessenheit und Gurus verleihen Zuversicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession by a god, spirit or drug is said to let one do what one would not normally feel able to, as, in part, does having a guru; such figures supply the confidence to walk the tightrope. Hine adds that sanity is located outside, not in one's head."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine adds that sanity lies 'out there' rather than in one's head."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 7 (Gods & Gurus); read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPossessionByEntity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession by an entity"@en, "Besessenheit durch eine Wesenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allow oneself to be possessed by a god, spirit or drug; no procedure given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 7 (Gods & Gurus); read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDaringBeyondOrdinaryAbility a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doing what one would not ordinarily dare"@en, "Tun, was man sich gewöhnlich nicht zutraut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under possession or a guru's backing one can act beyond one's ordinary sense of ability."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 7 (Gods & Gurus); read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcPossessionYieldsDaring a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Possession yields extraordinary confidence"@en, "Besessenheit ergibt außergewöhnliche Zuversicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession lets one do what one would not otherwise feel able to."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPossessionByEntity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDaringBeyondOrdinaryAbility ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 7 (Gods & Gurus); read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcStreetLevelTricksterMagick a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magick as street-level trickster activity"@en, "Magie als Straßenkunst des Tricksters"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contrary to the books, magick is called a street-level, even gutter-level activity following the trickster's zig-zag route (Crowley, Cagliostro, Simon Magus); chaos is laughing matter, and Harpo Marx shows true magick in action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 7 (Gods & Gurus); read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcTricksterSkills a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Trickster skills"@en, "Tricksterfertigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Learn juggling, mime and conjuring tricks; pass the hat round and raise a laugh."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 7 (Gods & Gurus); read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcStudyingChaoticAttractors a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying chaotic attractors"@en, "Chaotische Attraktoren studieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one meets a person around whom weirdness constantly happens, study them carefully, from a safe distance, to learn from them; such people are said to have a strange, mighty power they are often unaware of or embarrassed by."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 8; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcChaoticAttractorsDistanceCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Observe chaotic attractors from a safe distance"@en, "Chaotische Attraktoren aus sicherer Entfernung beobachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "People who draw weirdness around them should be studied, but preferably from a safe distance."@en ;
    skos:note "Said half-jokingly in parentheses."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicOrcStudyingChaoticAttractors ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 8; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDiaryEssential a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Diary held essential"@en, "Tagebuch gilt als unerlässlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping a diary of experiences and experiments is said to be generally held essential, because what is not written down after a working is likely to be forgotten."@en ;
    skos:note "The source says the diary is 'generally considered' essential and gives the loss of unrecorded insight as the reason; the dependent step is the keeping of insights from a working."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMagicalDiary ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicOrcRetainingAndRecallingInsight ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "A flash of insight after a ritual that is not written down will probably be forgotten, and that piece of wisdom is then lost for good." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 10; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMagicalDiary a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping a magical diary"@en, "Führen eines magischen Tagebuchs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep a record of experiences and experiments that charts progress, failures, experiments and insights; after each working write a summary of it, without censoring one's thoughts, changing the names of other participants to protect them."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondAMagicalDiary (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 practice gives a fixed entry (what, how long, where, weather, moon phase, how it went, ideas) and suggests keeping it as if for inspection; the 1992 text asks for a summary written up after each working, uncensored, with the names of other participants changed, and says the diary is held essential despite chaos magic's spontaneous image."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 10; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDiaryYieldsRecall a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Diary yields record, discipline and recall"@en, "Tagebuch ergibt Aufzeichnung, Disziplin und Erinnerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The diary charts progress and brings discipline and fresh recall."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondADiaryYieldsProgress (Condensed Chaos, 1995): In 1995 the diary yields visible progress and lets old ideas be taken up again; in 1992 it yields the keeping of insight, discipline, and recall in the act of writing up."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMagicalDiary ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcRetainingAndRecallingInsight ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 10; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcUnrecordedInsightLostCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unrecorded insights are lost"@en, "Nicht aufgezeichnete Einsichten gehen verloren"@de ;
    skos:definition "A flash of illumination after a ritual that is not written down will probably be forgotten for good."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMagicalDiary ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 10; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcRetainingAndRecallingInsight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Retaining insights and recalling overlooked details"@en, "Einsichten bewahren und Übersehenes erinnern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The written record keeps insights that would otherwise be forgotten; Hine adds that writing up a working often brings back things he had not noticed, and that the diary is a good discipline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Basic Exercises, item 10; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Conclusions
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcNoDefinitiveBooks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No definitive books; weave your own path"@en, "Keine maßgeblichen Bücher; den eigenen Weg weben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine stresses the booklet gives only his own ideas filtered through his experience; there are no definitive Chaos texts and no tradition to shelter in and escape the duty to be creative. Chaos magick demands that one weave one's own path of development, largely as one sees fit."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the method is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Conclusions; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcNoSetEndPoint a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No set goal or end-point"@en, "Kein festgelegtes Ziel oder Endpunkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chaos magick is said to have no distinct path leading somewhere, no promised illumination-bliss and no declared aim; any end-point is for each practitioner to decide and discover."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Conclusions; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcPlayingWithMagickCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "\"Playing with magick\" without deeper understanding"@en, "„Mit Magie spielen“ ohne tieferes Verständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Critics inside and outside the Chaos corpus are reported to point out a tendency to sample systems like ice-cream flavours, trying rituals and techniques with no grasp of how the experiences fit together; Hine does not reject the point."@en ;
    skos:note "Reported criticism from unnamed critics."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicOrcNoDefinitiveBooks ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Conclusions; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcNoRequirementToBeChaosMagician a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No set requirement to be a Chaos magician"@en, "Keine feste Voraussetzung, Chaosmagier zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked what one has to do to count as a Chaos magician, Hine says there is no answer: someone working Qabalah alone for a decade could call himself one, if he wished."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Conclusions; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcOpinionDogmaGlamourCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not mistake opinion for dogma or glamour for commitment"@en, "Meinung nicht mit Dogma, Glanz nicht mit Hingabe verwechseln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's closing warning is not to take opinion for dogma, nor glamour for commitment, adding that this too is only his opinion."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicOrcNoDefinitiveBooks ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Conclusions; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Fracture Lines
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcWillStoppedByWhy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Will stopped by asking why"@en, "Durch das Fragen nach dem Warum gestoppter Wille"@de ;
    skos:definition "The essay opens with Liber AL II.30: when will halts to ask why and invokes because, it stops and does nothing; obsession is presented as such a clouding of will."@en ;
    skos:note "Epigraph of the essay, from Crowley's Liber AL vel Legis II.30; Hine quotes it, he does not present it as received by himself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Fracture Lines; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcObsessionIntoTriangle a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Forcing an obsession into the triangle"@en, "Eine Obsession ins Dreieck zwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Withdraw into one's centre and circle, draw a triangle with a pen, drive the obsessing monster into it, and undo its strands of form: the weak moments, the longing and waiting, the desire fired by imagination from which it was made."@en ;
    skos:note "Narrated in lyrical first person; the classic evocation triangle used psychologically."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Fracture Lines; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcObsessionAsSelfMadeGolem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obsession as self-made demon or golem"@en, "Obsession als selbstgeschaffener Dämon oder Golem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine describes an obsession as a demon or golem he made from his own longings and failings, a story that clouded his will, which he then dismantles piece by piece; we are knots in a cord that can be untied."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Fracture Lines; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcCognitiveCutDown a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting down obsessive thoughts"@en, "Obsessive Gedanken zurückschneiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Analyse ruthlessly the thoughts and feelings tied to the situation and cut them down by vipassana, banishing or a similar strategy."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCCognitiveCutDown (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 practice cuts thoughts down by self-assessment, banishing or the like; the 1992 text names vipassana as the first means."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Fracture Lines, item 1; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPhysiologicalStilling a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stilling the body against obsessive anxiety"@en, "Den Körper gegen obsessive Angst beruhigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calm the anxious reactions of pulse, muscle tension and blood pressure by relaxation and pranayama."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCPhysiologicalStilling (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 practice stills the body by relaxation and meditation; the 1992 text names relaxation and pranayama."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Fracture Lines, item 2; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHineObsessionDissolvedYield a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Hine's obsession dissolved (anecdote)"@en, "Hines Obsession löste sich auf (Anekdote)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desperate, Hine turned to a friend, which he calls magick in itself; an I Ching reading pointing to action and non-action undid his self-doubt, pranayama removed most physical tension, and the monster shrank and dissolved into mirrored shards; the remaining clues no longer frighten him."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's report of his own case; turning to a friend for help he calls magick enough in itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBehavioralComponent, pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPhysiologicalStilling ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicCondCFreedomFromObsession ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Fracture Lines; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Howling
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcBabblogue a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Babblogue"@en, "Der Babblogue"@de ;
    skos:definition "Defined as a willed disordering of the senses, an orchestrated personal din and a descent into the subconscious in order to face and bind the lurkers there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHowlingPersonalApproach a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A personal approach, not a model"@en, "Ein persönlicher Ansatz, kein Vorbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine offers the account of exploring his own demons by a self-developed approach not to impose it but to help other experimenters, and disclaims invalidating traditional goetic magic, which simply does not suit him."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the method is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcBlackBookAndBookOfBlunders a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Compiling the black book and book of blunders"@en, "Anlegen des schwarzen Buches und des Buchs der Patzer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write a dissection of oneself: habits, faults, hopes, ideals, what one is, wishes to be or rejects, likes and revulsions; add positive, neutral and negative self-portraits in the third person, a CV and an obituary; then a book of every mistake and embarrassing memory, with old school reports, painful letters and photographs."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondCBookOfBlunders (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 practice is a book of painful, guilty or embarrassing episodes written without wallowing; the 1992 text prefaces it with a 'black book' dissecting the self, third-person self-portraits (positive, neutral, negative), a CV and an obituary, and adds school reports, letters and photographs to the book of blunders, all as material for the Howling operation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcScrambledPersonalityTapes a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Scrambled personality tapes"@en, "Verwürfelte Persönlichkeitsbänder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Read selected extracts of the self-catalogue onto tapes, then scramble the tapes into cut-up sequences; later replayed as auditory sigils raising emotional storms."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcPsychicSurgery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychic surgery: breaking and remoulding the self"@en, "Psychische Chirurgie: Zerbrechen und Neuformen des Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The cut-up work is described as a deliberate psychic surgery, breaking the vessel in order to remould it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCutUpTapesYieldPsychicSurgery a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cut-up tapes aim at psychic surgery"@en, "Cut-up-Bänder zielen auf psychische Chirurgie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The scrambled tapes are intended to smash and remould the self."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcScrambledPersonalityTapes, pmp:ChaosMagicOrcBlackBookAndBookOfBlunders ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcPsychicSurgery ;
