pmc:ChaosMagicOrcRiskingInsanityAloneCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Risking insanity alone without banishings"@en, "Wahnsinn riskieren, allein und ohne Bannungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine frames the work as a descent into the labyrinth with only the thinnest cord to map it, asking himself why he risks insanity and goes alone without tried rituals and banishings."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicOrcFloodingAndVomiting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDistrustOfOldGrimoires a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Distrust of the old grimoires"@en, "Misstrauen gegenüber den alten Grimoires"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked why he worked alone without tested rituals and banishings, Hine says he does not trust the old books, mocking mad monks, Necronomicons and forbidden knowledge sold cheaply in paperback, and chose to compile a living grimoire instead."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the grimoires he mocks are named by type, not cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMaslowDemonHierarchy a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Maslow-based demon hierarchy"@en, "Dämonenhierarchie nach Maslow"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine devised a hierarchy of demons modelled on Abraham Maslow's work, ranging from survival through ego to abstract demons; the deeper the level, the more primal the desires."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's own system adapted from Maslow. The text says deeper means more primal, so the listed order runs from most to least primal."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSurvivalDemonsNaming ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicOrcEgoDemonsNaming ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAbstractDemonsNaming ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine's hierarchy of demons runs from survival demons through ego demons to abstract demons, and the text says the deeper the level, the more primal the desires; a demon's level is therefore read from its place, the first place being the deepest and most primal and the last the most abstract." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

