pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPsychographs a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cohering images into psychographs"@en, "Bilder zu Psychographen verdichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give the demons shape by finger-painting, modelling clay blended with excreta and bodily fluids, sculpting with broken glass, and by sigils, automatic writing and free line-drawing; the products (psychographs) pile up in the temple."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcPsychographsFallShortFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychographs fall short of the visions"@en, "Psychographen bleiben hinter den Visionen zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine reports that the psychographs fell far short of the visions around him; he smashed them with a hammer and collapsed exhausted and retching."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the psychographs come nowhere near the visions Hine sees about him, and he smashes them. The cause is put on the operator's means of giving shape to what he sees; no deadline and no rate. The failure is the turning point of the operation: the howling of names (pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHowledNamesReceiving) follows at once. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPsychographs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHowledNamesReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Names howled from the throat"@en, "Aus der Kehle geheulte Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the breaking point, with a wrenching sensation in his head, Hine began to howl names that erupted from his throat, given as a string of barbarous syllables forming a section heading."@en ;
    skos:note "Speaker not identified; the names arise unbidden, implicitly from the evoked demons."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Phil Hine, alone in his temple at the climax of the Howling operation" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Unnamed; the names erupt from Hine's own throat, and the text does not say from whom they come" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "After about five days without sleep, sensory overload and fasting, Hine smashes his psychographs and collapses; with a wrenching sensation in his head he begins to howl names, which the text prints as a section heading of barbarous syllables." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcHowlYieldsCalmDetachment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The howl yields calm detachment"@en, "Das Heulen ergibt ruhige Distanz"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the climax (the jackals that rushed in all wore his face) Hine felt calm and detached."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcFloodingAndVomiting, pmp:ChaosMagicOrcOverloadDeprivationGnosis ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCalmDetachment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Howling; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCalmDetachment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Calm detachment after the howl"@en, "Ruhige Distanz nach dem Heulen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine came back with a calm detachment, momentarily emptied of feeling, able to look at his work as if it were not his."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
