    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcReticularFormationCensor a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reticular Formation as censor; cortical dampening"@en, "Formatio reticularis als Zensor; kortikale Dämpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The brain-stem Reticular Formation decides which sensory input reaches the higher centres (as when sleepers ignore familiar noise but wake to a new one). A single unchanging input damps it, which inhibits the cortex and focuses consciousness; a high neural coherence, as Karl Pribram postulated, seems to follow, with less brain noise."@en ;
    skos:note "Draws on Karl Pribram."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcOnePointedYieldsSubtlePerception a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Habituation yields subtle perception"@en, "Habituation ergibt feine Wahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One-pointed techniques, via cortical dampening and coherence, are said to sharpen perception of subtle experience."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcOnePointedFocusing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSubtlePatternPerception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSubtlePatternPerception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clearer perception of subtle patterns"@en, "Klarere Wahrnehmung feiner Muster"@de ;
    skos:definition "With less neural noise, ordinarily indistinct patterns become clear, one is more aware of the surroundings and perceives subtler aspects of experience; the more ordered cortical activity, the wider the totality of experience one is aware of."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcOverstimulationReducesAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Over-stimulation reduces awareness"@en, "Überstimulation verringert Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conversely, greater over-stimulation of the cortex brings more neural noise arises and the less aware one is of one's environment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDishabituatedAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dishabituated awareness"@en, "Dishabituierte Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Research is reported to show that advanced practitioners do not habituate to background noise and keep full awareness of automatic actions; the practices are said to dishabituate the Reticular Formation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMetanoia a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Metanoia: whole-field awareness practices"@en, "Metanoia: Praktiken der Gesamtfeld-Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of one-pointedness, widen awareness until one is continuously aware of the whole field of inner and outer experience, e.g. Tantric vipassana, Zen attention or Gurdjieff's self-remembering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMetanoiaYieldsDishabituation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Metanoia yields dishabituated awareness"@en, "Metanoia ergibt dishabituierte Bewusstheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whole-field practices are said to change neural patterning so that stimuli are no longer filtered out by habit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMetanoia ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcDishabituatedAwareness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcWorldBrighterAfterMeditationSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "World appears brighter after meditation"@en, "Die Welt erscheint nach der Meditation heller"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a meditation session the world appears brighter or newer, explained as neural pulse rates first damped and then restimulated to fire faster than normal."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: once a meditation session is over the world looks brighter or newer, explained by neural firing first damped and then restimulated above its normal rate. Judged by the practitioner alone, at once after the session; no deadline and no rate. It concerns pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMetanoia and pmp:ChaosMagicOrcOnePointedFocusing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcBohmHolisticUniverse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Holistic universe and ordered action (Bohm)"@en, "Holistisches Universum und geordnetes Handeln (Bohm)"@de ;
    skos:definition "David Bohm is reported to hold that conceiving the universe as whole instead of fragmented would make the mind move likewise and produce ordered action toward the whole; Hine says his experience of learning that the universe is magical bears this out."@en ;
    skos:note "Reports physicist David Bohm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Technical Ecstacy; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Of Madness & Mystic Journeys
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSchizophreniaAndMysticJourney a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Schizophrenia and the mystic journey"@en, "Schizophrenie und die mystische Reise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the anti-psychiatrists Laing and Cooper, schizophrenia is likened to the mystic and shamanic inner journey, with shared reports of lost agency, lost ego boundary and feeling set apart; but Hine insists that the initiate or shaman acts as the active, fearless agent, which the person in schizophrenia rarely is."@en ;
    skos:note "Reports R.D. Laing and David Cooper; Hine qualifies their view."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Of Madness & Mystic Journeys; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcVestibularNuclei a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensory integration and the vestibular nuclei"@en, "Sensorische Integration und die Vestibulariskerne"@de ;
    skos:definition "Research tied to Sensory Integration therapy is said to show that schizophrenic problems of selecting important input stem from abnormal function of the vestibular nuclei, which integrate the senses and relate to the Reticular Formation; deficits may be genetic or stress-induced. Certain neuroscientists regard subcortical activity as the key to altered states."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Of Madness & Mystic Journeys; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcEvolutionOrSystemsCrashCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "ASC as evolution or systems crash"@en, "Veränderter Bewusstseinszustand als Evolution oder Systemabsturz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some postulate that such experiences are genetically programmed, with individual experience deciding whether the program unfolds as an evolutionary step enhancing survival or as a systems crash."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicOrcSchizophreniaAndMysticJourney ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Of Madness & Mystic Journeys; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Illumination
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcGnosisYieldsIllumination a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Gnosis methods yield illumination"@en, "Gnosismethoden ergeben Erleuchtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carroll is cited defining illumination as the result of success with gnosis methods."@en ;
    skos:note "The practices joined are the gnosis techniques the text describes; the source of the claim is Carroll's definition as Hine quotes it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcOnePointedFocusing, pmp:ChaosMagicOrcMetanoia, pmp:ChaosMagicCondCTacNukeGnosis ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcIlluminationAfterCarroll ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Illumination; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcIlluminationAfterCarroll a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Illumination"@en, "Erleuchtung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illumination, defined after Carroll's Liber Null as the inspiration, enlightenment and liberation that result from success with gnosis methods, is called the goal sought worldwide through many psychotechnologies; it has been linked with LSD and similar drugs and may also come unbidden to people who neither know of it nor expect it."@en ;
    skos:note "Definition quoted from Pete Carroll, Liber Null."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIllumination (Condensed Chaos, 1995): The 1995 node calls illumination the peak of initiation through death and rebirth; the 1992 essay defines it with Carroll's Liber Null as the inspiration, enlightenment and liberation that follow success with gnosis methods, and names it the goal of many psychotechnologies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Illumination; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# The conditioned reflex
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMassAcceptableMagickCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mass-acceptable magick loses its power"@en, "Massentaugliche Magie verliert ihre Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enlightenment has been turned into a status marker; a magick acceptable to mass culture is said to lose its transformative power and prop up the status quo, sacrificing evolution to security."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicOrcIlluminationAfterCarroll ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), The conditioned reflex; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .


#
# Ego
#

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcAgainstHigherLowerSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the New Age Higher/Lower Self"@en, "Gegen das New-Age-Höhere/Niedere Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine disputes the New Age aim of removing or transcending the ego in favour of a Higher Self, arguing that the ego concept from psychoanalytic cults keeps up the mind-body split and that the Higher-Lower Self fiction keeps spirituality apart from daily life."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read: the New Age writers he opposes are not named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Ego; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcShaktisNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Shaktis"@en, "Shaktis"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the Tantric picture adopted by Hine, Shaktis are the desire-complexes making up the self."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Shaktis" ;
    pm:nameRole "desire-complexes within the self" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Ego; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcShivaKiaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Shiva / Kia"@en, "Shiva / Kia"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shiva, or Kia, is held to be the divine spark of consciousness with which the Shaktis interact."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Shiva", "Kia" ;
    pm:nameRole "divine spark of consciousness" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Ego; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPsychotropicDrugs a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychotropic drugs for altered states"@en, "Psychotrope Drogen für veränderte Zustände"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use of drugs such as mescaline or peyote is named as one of the oldest and most controversial means of inducing altered states; no procedure is given."@en ;
    skos:note "Only the use is named; no steps are given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Ego; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcPsychotropicsYieldIllumination a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Psychotropics yield illumination effects"@en, "Psychotropika ergeben Erleuchtungswirkungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Research is reported to show that users of psychotropics have the same effects as illumination reached by other techniques."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPsychotropicDrugs ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicOrcIlluminationAfterCarroll ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Ego; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcIntegrationAfterExperience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Integration after the experience"@en, "Integration nach der Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing the American researcher W.N. Pankhe, Hine says the most demanding work may follow a drug-induced experience of illumination: fitting it into everyday life."@en ;
    skos:note "Recorded as a claim and not as a prerequisite: the text names no separate step of integration that could be a node."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Oven-Ready Chaos, version 1.4 (on-line edition typeset by the author, text of 1992 first published by Chaos International as Condensed Chaos), Ego; read in the full text of the TealDOC conversion of 2000" .

pmc:ChaosMagicOrcLSDBrainwashingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "LSD studied as brainwashing agent"@en, "LSD als Gehirnwäschemittel untersucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine recalls that the CIA investigated LSD in the 1950s as a possible brainwashing agent."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicOrcPsychotropicDrugs ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:OvenReadyChaos ;
